From e1cd0c2cec04f546e72ff221335e249e9b63b197 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Skippy <build@skippy.local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:35:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] models: shape dflash inkling2 zonos3 builders for stage
 proofs

The stage rewriter could not prove the new upstream draft builders:
graph_base owns shared-input setup with no body of its own, draft token
tables resolve through a helper call the proof cannot follow, Inkling 2
kept its token embedding in a helper while the layer loop stayed in the
constructor, Inkling2 Loop reached several remote helpers, and Zonos 3
carried a differently named local through its layer loop.

- graph_base prepares the shared inputs through prepare_decoder_inputs,
  called by each derived body; build_layers takes the resolved table
- each draft body resolves the token table inline with the ctx_other
  fallback, the shape this queue carried before the upstream refactor
- build_inputs keeps only the shared inputs; the inkling2 constructors
  own their token embedding producer
- the Inkling2 Loop core pass moves to build_core_pass
- zonos3 names its loop-carried local after the embedding activation

No graph changes: the same nodes are built in the same order.
